  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/sinobdella-sinensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>A small spiny eel that rarely grows larger than 20 cm. It is the only species in its genus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/sinobdella-sinensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>The species inhabits China and parts of Vietnam.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/sinobdella-sinensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>According to its origin, care in unheated aquariums is recommended. Choose soft sand as substrate, in which the spiny eels like to dig themselves in. If this possibility is missing, the spiny eels tend to get skin infections.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/sinobdella-sinensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Frozen and live food of suitable size is taken, especially worm food. It is assumed that settled animals also feed on granules, but there is still a lack of experience.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/sinobdella-sinensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>Among each other, the animals are peaceful, as is known from spiny eels generally. Small fishes are potential prey; other, bigger species are not considered further.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/22-spiny-eels/sinobdella-sinensis-2/",
      "html": "<p>In Sinobdella the dorsal, caudal and anal fins are fused together, which in Asian spiny eels is otherwise a sign of large species. The animals differ from all other spiny eels in the peculiar nose/nozzle region. The shining white edge of the anal fin is an eye-catching characteristic. The coloration is individually very variable.</p>"
    }
  ],
